  {"id":"13dc4890-f9ab-4080-8b08-df088db923ab","term":"Vocal expansion","verdict":"MINOR","suggestions":[{"field":"common_mistakes","severity":"Medium","issue":"The mistake 'Using too fast an attack so the gate chatters on and off' misattributes the cause of chatter to attack time. Web-verified via Sound On Sound (soundonsound.com, 'Advanced Gating Techniques: Part 1'): gate/expander chatter occurs when the signal hovers around the threshold with too-fast RELEASE times, and is cured with hold time and hysteresis — attack controls only how fast the gate opens and does not itself cause chatter. Note the term 'Vocal gating' in this same packet correctly attributes chatter to release.","suggestion":"Change to 'Using too fast a release (with no hold time or hysteresis), so the expander/gate chatters on and off when the signal hovers near the threshold.'"}]},
